{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require all pet microchip databases to update contact details free of charge",
        "additional_details": "Owners/keepers are legally required to keep microchip details current, or risk a \u00a3500 fine - yet the 24 pet microchip databases charge inconsistent fees, from free to up to \u00a330 one-off payments to tiered subscriptions. I am concerned this confuses owners and discourages updates. If it\u2019s a legal duty, why should people pay to comply with it? Making updates free could remove a real barrier, ensuring the system works as intended for animal welfare and public safety. \r\n\r\nMake Chips Count - Pet Theft Reform",
        "background": "Require all pet microchip databases to let owners/keepers update contact details free of charge. Keeping microchip records accurate is a legal duty. We think no one should have to pay to comply with it. Free, clearly-advertised updates mean more lost pets reunited with their owners.",
